course: dictionary
lesson: 14020
title: A magnifier makes things bigger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A magnifier is a tool that makes things look bigger than they really are. Usually it is a lens, a curved piece of clear glass or plastic. «Sam used a magnifier to look at the ant's tiny legs.» The clue is tiny legs: a magnifier helps you see very small things up close.
explain: The word can also mean something on a computer. «Mum turned on the magnifier so the words on the screen were easier to read.» The clues are screen and easier to read: here the magnifier makes part of the screen bigger.
explain: Always check the context to see which meaning fits. In science, a magnifier helps you look closely at leaves, insects and soil. Be careful: a magnifier can focus sunlight and start a fire, so never point it at the sun or at people.
fact: A magnifier is a tool, usually a lens, that makes things look bigger.
fact: On a computer, a magnifier is a program that makes part of the screen bigger.
fact: In science, a magnifier (hand lens) helps you look closely at insects, leaves and soil.
fact: Never point a magnifier at the sun or at people: it can focus sunlight and start a fire.
exercise: «Sam used a magnifier to look at the ant's tiny legs.» What is a magnifier? | A small insect | A type of ruler | *A tool that makes things look bigger | A tool that makes things look smaller
exercise: «Mum turned on the magnifier so the words on the screen were easier to read.» On a computer, what does a magnifier do? | It changes the colour of the whole screen | *It makes part of the screen bigger | It turns the computer off | It types the words for you
exercise: Why should you never point a magnifier at the sun? | It makes the sky go dark | It makes the sun look smaller | *It can focus sunlight and start a fire | It cools the sun down
test: In science, what might you use a magnifier to look at? | *Leaves, insects and soil | Planes and rockets | Cars on the road | Clouds in the sky
test: In «The magnifier made the tiny flower look much bigger», what does magnifier mean? | A type of pen | *A tool that makes things look bigger | A flower | A tiny insect
exam: Which sentence uses magnifier correctly? | *Ravi held a magnifier over the leaf to see its tiny veins | Ella ate a magnifier for lunch | The magnifier was a sunny afternoon at the beach | Dad drove the magnifier to school
